# 8. PROFESSIONAL ENTRY TIMING VALIDATION

Too many late or early signals can make the entire platform unreliable.

Audit:

- Signal formation.
- Candidate detection.
- Confirmation time.
- Publication time.
- Entry eligibility.
- Actual simulated order trigger.

Distinguish:

### Early Candidate

Setup developing.

Not yet approved.

### Confirmed Setup

Strategy confirmation completed.

Still requires entry and risk feasibility checks.

### Approved Opportunity

Qualified under the signal policy.

May be waiting for entry.

### Triggered Trade

Simulated order actually filled under the execution model.

### Closed Trade

A real simulated trade outcome exists.

Do not label an approved-but-unfilled opportunity as a profitable trade.

Do not place historical entry signals before the necessary confirmation candle.

